CUDA Page Based Memory Coherence (Upcoming Maxwell Architecture)
The goal is to allow CUDA programs to pass pointers between CPU and GPU SMs in a cache coherent way without asking programmers to do explicit memory copies. Targetted for systems where we dont own the CPU. This uses faults to do page copies implicitly. 

My role is to drive/ scope out Linux kernel VM changes for page based DSM implementation along with identifing GPU hw changes to make this task optimal especially in improving GPU page fault latencies. Currently implementing proof of concepts / identifying memory access patterns for customer apps and doing perf estimates. So far I ve implemented MOESI in software to track page ownership between CPU(s)/GPU(s) and also implemented asynchronous page migrations using GPU's dma engines.

False sharing is a huge problem with this approach. Another team is investigating in parallel a weaker consistency model that uses explicit acquire/releases, I am helping them in a supporting role.


